// `while let Some(r) = o` over a PLACE moves its payload on the first iteration; the loop's back edge reads it again (rustc E0382). Twin of pass/bc_patown_whilelet_place_reinit_break, where `o` is re-assigned before the edge. PROBES.md 2026-09-06d: `if let` / `while let` / let-chains lower BY DELEGATION to lower_match (temp hoist, per-arm scrutinee move, arm drops, cond-move merge); the count is a destructor tally through a raw pointer.
package bc_patown_whilelet_place_scrut_loop_fail;

struct S { v: i64, i: *mut i64 }
impl Drop for S { fn drop(self: &mut S) { unsafe { *self.i = *self.i + self.v; } } }
fn eat(s: S) -> i64 { return s.v; }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut c: i64 = 0i64;
    let p: *mut i64 = &mut c;
    {
        let o: Option<S> = Option::Some(S { v: 1i64, i: p });
        let mut n: i64 = 0i64;
        while let Option::Some(r) = o { n = n + r.v; if n > 0i64 { break; } }
        if n != 1i64 { return 99i32; }
    }
    return c as i32;
}
